1
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:04,571
She's at the other side
of "God's hand."

2
00:00:05,805 --> 00:00:07,140
"Demon's hands."

3
00:00:07,207 --> 00:00:09,809
She is the Devil.

4
00:00:11,911 --> 00:00:15,448
- Hello. It's been a while.
- You're looking great.

5
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:19,686
Transfer to the 18th branch
in Kanazawa.

6
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:21,254
What can I do for you?

7
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:27,327
He will run for the chairperson's
election with my endorsement.

8
00:00:27,394 --> 00:00:30,330
You've endorsed Ebina
for the next election.

9
00:00:30,397 --> 00:00:32,465
Good. It's complete.

10
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:36,236
You'll be introduced
as Hiruma's successor.

11
00:00:36,302 --> 00:00:37,270
You did it, sir.

12
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:41,207
He's like my pupil.

13
00:00:41,841 --> 00:00:43,543
Hope it's not a one-side game.

14
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:48,214
- You bought a new horse.
- Kind of.

15
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:50,150
A horse?

16
00:01:03,997 --> 00:01:05,832
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

17
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:07,400
KAZUYO MABUCHI

18
00:01:08,268 --> 00:01:09,102
Hello.

19
00:01:27,687 --> 00:01:29,756
What's going on?

20
00:01:29,823 --> 00:01:32,292
They're telling us part-timers
to do operations today

21
00:01:32,358 --> 00:01:35,962
- due to the joint conference.
- It's complete. How many more?

22
00:01:36,029 --> 00:01:37,263
Six patients.

23
00:01:37,997 --> 00:01:41,601
We've done half.
Why don't you take a break?

24
00:01:45,038 --> 00:01:45,972
Next.

25
00:01:46,406 --> 00:01:48,842
Okay. I will follow you.

26
00:01:50,477 --> 00:01:53,913
This is a story
about a maverick female doctor.

27
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:57,150
University hospitals lost
their authorities.

28
00:01:57,784 --> 00:01:59,786
Medical care has become the world

29
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:03,423
where the strong prey on the weak.

30
00:02:04,991 --> 00:02:09,162
I'd like to introduce a surgeon
today at this joint conference of

31
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:12,999
the Dept. of Surgery
and internal Medicine.

32
00:02:13,066 --> 00:02:17,704
I'm sure you've heard
of his recent success,

33
00:02:18,538 --> 00:02:22,542
living kidney and small bowel
exchange transplant.

34
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:26,880
This is a world-class operation.

35
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:28,348
Without a doubt,

36
00:02:28,414 --> 00:02:31,384
he is a pride and hope
for Teito University Hospital.

37
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,319
Let me introduce him.

38
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:38,458
He is Shinobu Kondo, who is newly
appointed as a professor

39
00:02:38,525 --> 00:02:41,561
in the 2nd Surgery Department.

40
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:45,365
SHINOBU KONDO

41
00:02:45,431 --> 00:02:48,034
TAKASHI EBINA
PROFESSOR, 2ND SURGERY DEPT.

42
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:51,137
I'm Kondo.

43
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:56,509
I'm honored to take this position's
responsibility I assumed.

44
00:02:57,744 --> 00:03:01,181
I deeply thank
Executive Manager Hiruma,

45
00:03:01,748 --> 00:03:06,819
for my being appointed
to such a position.

46
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:08,188
Not at all.

47
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:14,327
Thanks. Good luck.

48
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:16,863
It's embarrassing to listen that.

49
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:21,000
Kondo is the leading candidate
for the chairperson.

50
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:25,438
Internal Medicine Dept.,
isn't he handsome?

51
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:29,075
I don't see someone like him
in your department.

52
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:30,944
Thanks, Kondo. You can go.

53
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:37,884
I also have someone that
I'd like to introduce to everyone.

54
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:45,024
Professor Takano?

55
00:03:45,091 --> 00:03:46,859
Wasn't he transferred to Ishikawa?

56
00:04:05,011 --> 00:04:08,047
This is Prof. Naoki Takano

57
00:04:08,114 --> 00:04:12,418
who is reassigned to
the 2nd Surgery Dept. as of today.

58
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:14,053
I'm Takano.

59
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,589
NAOKI TAKANO
PROFESSOR, 2ND SURGERY DEPT.

60
00:04:23,563 --> 00:04:24,797
Thank you.

61
00:04:27,133 --> 00:04:28,234
Phew, I'm starving.

62
00:04:28,568 --> 00:04:31,471
That's why I told you
to take a break.

63
00:04:31,804 --> 00:04:34,807
Next patient has a history
of chronic heart failure.

64
00:04:34,874 --> 00:04:38,211
- I'll do it fast. Prepare diuretic.
- Sure.

65
00:04:39,646 --> 00:04:40,513
OPERATION ROOM

66
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:44,917
To save this crisis
in the world of medical care,

67
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:48,821
a freelance doctor, in other words,
a maverick doctor, appeared.

68
00:04:52,358 --> 00:04:55,094
Prof. Takano published the thesis,

69
00:04:55,161 --> 00:04:58,865
was nominated for the Kluivert Prize
in a medical conference of Paris.

70
00:05:01,668 --> 00:05:02,835
What was the topic?

71
00:05:03,503 --> 00:05:06,773
FOLFIRINOX Therapy: preoperative

72
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:08,775
chemo for pancreatic cancer.

73
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:12,645
This research started
in this hospital.

74
00:05:12,712 --> 00:05:15,648
Still, the Surgery Dept. let him go

75
00:05:15,715 --> 00:05:18,951
because it didn't realize
how talented he is.

76
00:05:20,253 --> 00:05:21,921
That is rude of you to say that.

77
00:05:23,856 --> 00:05:26,192
It's been a while, Ebina.

78
00:05:26,893 --> 00:05:27,927
Yes, sir.

79
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:30,096
Hope you improved your skill.

80
00:05:35,101 --> 00:05:38,404
I'd like to take this opportunity
to tell you.

81
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:44,911
I, Naoki Takano, will run
for the next chairperson's election.

82
00:05:44,977 --> 00:05:50,450
I intend to change completely
the corrupt the 2nd Surgery Dept.

83
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:52,652
Takano.

84
00:05:52,719 --> 00:05:56,389
You need to mind your language.

85
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:01,961
What do you mean by corrupt?

86
00:06:02,929 --> 00:06:05,732
It's completely unfounded.

87
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:11,537
Don't be conceited for only
being a nominee for Kluivert.

88
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:17,643
In any case, we want fairness
in the election for the chairperson.

89
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:22,715
May I take this as a declaration
of war from you

90
00:06:22,782 --> 00:06:24,884
and the rest of the staff

91
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:29,222
in the Internal Medicine Department?

92
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:34,427
As you please.

93
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:36,496
Understood.

94
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:41,768
We'll take advantage of this election,
and straighten things out.

95
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:46,272
I don't care
if it's straight or not.

96
00:06:47,173 --> 00:06:49,776
I need an assistant.
Can someone help?

97
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:54,714
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

98
00:06:56,015 --> 00:06:59,452
- That's not important.
- I don't think this one is!

99
00:06:59,519 --> 00:07:03,222
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

100
00:07:03,723 --> 00:07:08,861
<i>Her medical certifications and on-the-job</i>
<i>experience are her only weapons.</i>

101
00:07:10,029 --> 00:07:12,498
Surgeon Michiko Daimon,

102
00:07:13,299 --> 00:07:16,169
also known as Doctor-X.

103
00:07:48,334 --> 00:07:50,570
- May I sit here?
- Go ahead.

104
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:55,274
Nobody wants to sit here.
I wonder why.

105
00:07:55,908 --> 00:07:57,143
Because you look scary.

106
00:07:59,378 --> 00:08:03,216
Everyone looked at me
like that since I was young.

107
00:08:04,217 --> 00:08:05,418
It really annoys me.

108
00:08:07,587 --> 00:08:09,655
- Was that on the menu?
- This one?

109
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:12,725
This is a special order.

110
00:08:14,393 --> 00:08:17,697
I have it delivered
from a famous restaurant.

111
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:22,869
You're in a white gown.

112
00:08:22,935 --> 00:08:26,372
- Which department do you work for?
- I'm a freelance surgeon.

113
00:08:26,439 --> 00:08:29,342
You're a part-timer?

114
00:08:29,408 --> 00:08:32,812
No, no. I'm a freelance surgeon.

115
00:08:32,879 --> 00:08:36,048
It doesn't matter which one.

116
00:08:36,115 --> 00:08:38,417
A surgeon just needs a skill.

117
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:42,154
Are you visiting someone?

118
00:08:42,221 --> 00:08:45,625
Me? I have cancer.

119
00:08:46,659 --> 00:08:51,364
My doctor tells me
that I have 50/50 chance.

120
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:52,265
I'll operate.

121
00:08:52,732 --> 00:08:56,435
But I'm not worried too much.

122
00:08:56,502 --> 00:08:59,705
When a doctor says it's 50/50,

123
00:08:59,772 --> 00:09:03,142
I have a higher chance
to be cured by 20/80.

124
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:05,244
I can cure you 100%.

125
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:10,416
Your joke is too far-fetched.

126
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:12,051
This is not a joke.

127
00:09:14,287 --> 00:09:18,925
You change the 2nd Surgery Dept.
by returning as a chairperson?

128
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:22,161
That was my intention
for coming back.

129
00:09:23,129 --> 00:09:26,399
I am determined to
destroy Professor Hiruma.

130
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:30,903
Do you have a plan?

131
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:34,607
Yes. I will perform
in this hospital,

132
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:37,810
the research of FOLFIRINOX Therapy.

133
00:09:37,877 --> 00:09:39,912
Great Idea.

134
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:45,051
That would definitely
blow away the Hiruma camp.

135
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:49,689
But is there
such a flexible patient?

136
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:53,559
I transferred her from
the 18th branch in Kanazawa today.

137
00:09:55,895 --> 00:09:58,130
The patient Prof. Takano transferred

138
00:09:58,631 --> 00:10:02,768
is the mother of Mr. Asai, Director
General of Health Policy Bureau.

139
00:10:02,835 --> 00:10:03,936
What?

140
00:10:04,570 --> 00:10:06,305
If we make Mr. Asai upset,

141
00:10:06,806 --> 00:10:08,741
no hospital can survive.

142
00:10:09,175 --> 00:10:11,644
Due to the malpractice
of our branch,

143
00:10:12,078 --> 00:10:15,014
our crown as advanced treatment
was taken away.

144
00:10:15,081 --> 00:10:16,816
Don't remind me.

145
00:10:16,882 --> 00:10:17,917
I apologize.

146
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,053
Please let me be
in charge of that patient.

147
00:10:22,355 --> 00:10:25,524
I know you can do it. Please.

148
00:10:26,192 --> 00:10:27,526
Please appoint me.

149
00:10:29,195 --> 00:10:32,865
You can't cut each other's throats.

150
00:10:35,835 --> 00:10:37,570
We are the mainstream
of this hospital.

151
00:10:39,872 --> 00:10:42,341
We should never take a backseat.

152
00:10:45,911 --> 00:10:50,916
Either of you must assume
the position of the chairperson.

153
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:53,052
- Understood?
- Yes, sir.

154
00:10:55,421 --> 00:10:56,889
The condition of the patient?

155
00:11:00,092 --> 00:11:03,162
What kind of education

156
00:11:03,229 --> 00:11:07,199
do you give to your part-timers?

157
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,434
Michiko.

158
00:11:09,235 --> 00:11:11,303
What did you do this time?

159
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:17,343
She tried to do business
personally with our special patient.

160
00:11:18,144 --> 00:11:21,380
Oh, that "eel" lady? I see.

161
00:11:21,947 --> 00:11:24,817
- We received a complaint.
- What kind?

162
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:30,956
"An overly confident doctor will
prompt fears to a patient."

163
00:11:31,023 --> 00:11:32,258
Wow.

164
00:11:32,324 --> 00:11:34,060
We are sorry.

165
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:38,931
I will apologize
to the patient in person tomorrow.

166
00:11:38,998 --> 00:11:41,033
And who is the patient?

167
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:45,905
I won't fall for that.

168
00:11:45,971 --> 00:11:48,507
You're trying to do business again.

169
00:11:48,574 --> 00:11:50,576
No way.

170
00:11:50,643 --> 00:11:52,011
You can't trick me.

171
00:11:52,078 --> 00:11:53,713
Can we play?

172
00:11:53,779 --> 00:11:56,515
Here, there are four of us.

173
00:11:57,516 --> 00:11:59,452
- Four?
- Won't you join us?

174
00:11:59,518 --> 00:12:01,754
- Let's play.
- Yes.

175
00:12:01,821 --> 00:12:05,458
I said you can't trick me.

176
00:12:06,659 --> 00:12:07,960
Pon!

177
00:12:10,329 --> 00:12:15,434
The one who succeeds
in Mr. Asai's mother's surgery

178
00:12:15,501 --> 00:12:18,738
will take the lead in
the chairperson's election.

179
00:12:18,804 --> 00:12:20,940
It's between us.
Don't tell on others.

180
00:12:23,275 --> 00:12:24,877
Pon.

181
00:12:26,178 --> 00:12:27,847
Which one is in the lead?

182
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:30,616
It's definitely Mabuchi camp,
for Prof. Takano's feat.

183
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:32,952
He transferred Mr. Asai's

184
00:12:34,286 --> 00:12:38,824
mother from Kanazawa.

185
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:44,730
- It's just between us.
- What's her disease?

186
00:12:44,797 --> 00:12:47,533
- I can't tell you that.
- Come on.

187
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,336
I don't know what to do. Ton.

188
00:12:50,402 --> 00:12:52,972
Ron! The big four winds. Yakuman!

189
00:12:53,038 --> 00:12:54,473
What the heck?

190
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,808
Thank you.

191
00:12:55,875 --> 00:12:58,878
How could you put out Ton here?

192
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:02,548
He's too good.
I've never met such a strong player.

193
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:06,051
- Is that so?
- Can you teach us every day?

194
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:08,254
Then should I come here every day?

195
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:12,158
- I'm so excited!
- I love strong men.

196
00:13:13,526 --> 00:13:15,327
And what is her disease?

197
00:13:18,731 --> 00:13:21,400
You win.

198
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:28,440
Don't tell anyone.

199
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:30,142
Yes, sir.

200
00:13:30,209 --> 00:13:34,280
It's pancreatic cancer,
the stage IV-A. It's very serious.

201
00:13:35,114 --> 00:13:36,549
The surgery is difficult.

202
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:43,589
Takano will team up with medicine
and apply the combined therapy.

203
00:13:44,857 --> 00:13:47,893
We should stick to the surgical

204
00:13:48,794 --> 00:13:50,763
treatment without the medicine.

205
00:13:51,797 --> 00:13:52,832
I agree.

206
00:13:55,601 --> 00:13:58,037
Extended resection
of pancreatic head?

207
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:02,408
Let's do that.

208
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,878
But, what about you?

209
00:14:07,813 --> 00:14:08,814
I'll be your assistant.

210
00:14:11,383 --> 00:14:12,518
You'll be the surgeon.

211
00:14:15,087 --> 00:14:19,792
However, I'm not giving up
to become a chairperson.

212
00:14:24,263 --> 00:14:25,865
I'll be running against you.

213
00:14:29,935 --> 00:14:33,772
But we have an enemy
we need to destroy.

214
00:14:35,774 --> 00:14:36,842
I understand.

215
00:14:39,411 --> 00:14:43,916
Let's eliminate our enemy
in front of us now.

216
00:14:47,286 --> 00:14:48,153
Yes, sir.

217
00:14:52,992 --> 00:14:54,927
TEITO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

218
00:14:54,994 --> 00:14:56,762
The 2nd Surgery Department

219
00:14:57,096 --> 00:15:00,199
recommends extended resection
of pancreatic head.

220
00:15:02,268 --> 00:15:03,769
Thank you, Dr. Kondo.

221
00:15:04,136 --> 00:15:07,273
I think it's a brilliant idea.

222
00:15:08,641 --> 00:15:11,844
What do you think,
Executive Manager Mabuchi?

223
00:15:12,544 --> 00:15:16,181
It's the best the Surgery Dept.
takes over to treat this patient.

224
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:22,254
with no help from
Internal Medicine Department.

225
00:15:23,055 --> 00:15:26,358
That's the limit of
the Surgery Dept.

226
00:15:32,064 --> 00:15:35,034
Vascular and nerve plexus
invasion of cancer cells

227
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,636
can't be removed by surgery alone.

228
00:15:37,703 --> 00:15:40,306
I recommend the FOLFIRINOX Therapy

229
00:15:40,372 --> 00:15:42,775
with the Internal Medicine.

230
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:45,611
Sir.

231
00:15:47,446 --> 00:15:52,384
I can avoid such a pain process
and remove the entire nerve plexus.

232
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:57,690
Those two surgeons will
get timid removing it.

233
00:15:57,756 --> 00:16:00,125
The effect of FOLFIRINOX
depends on a patient.

234
00:16:10,102 --> 00:16:11,070
What?

235
00:16:14,907 --> 00:16:15,908
What is it?

236
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:17,142
Daimon.

237
00:16:18,477 --> 00:16:20,312
I ask you one question.

238
00:16:22,514 --> 00:16:27,686
What all patients want the most is
the complete removal of cancer.

239
00:16:29,421 --> 00:16:32,458
And you can do it, right?

240
00:16:36,028 --> 00:16:37,997
I never fail.

241
00:16:40,399 --> 00:16:42,401
Did you hear that, everyone?

242
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:44,770
Did you?

243
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:52,111
She just told me
that she never fails.

244
00:16:52,911 --> 00:16:54,079
How wonderful.

245
00:16:56,382 --> 00:16:57,983
We let her,

246
00:16:58,784 --> 00:17:02,121
Michiko Daimon
of the 2nd Surgery Department,

247
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:08,027
be in charge of our special patient.

248
00:17:08,961 --> 00:17:13,499
What do you think everyone?

249
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:16,135
- Yes sir.
- Yes, sir.

250
00:17:25,077 --> 00:17:26,478
We won in the last minute.

251
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:29,815
- We should stick to Hiruma camp.
- Yes, sir.

252
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:52,037
I'm coming in.

253
00:18:02,014 --> 00:18:04,383
HISAE ASAI

254
00:18:04,450 --> 00:18:06,051
You've got to be kidding.

255
00:18:06,118 --> 00:18:10,355
No, I'm not kidding.
I'm in charge of your operation.

256
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:13,358
I came here from Kanazawa

257
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,861
to have Dr. Takano treat me.

258
00:18:16,662 --> 00:18:19,665
Call him right away.

259
00:18:20,566 --> 00:18:22,534
Dr. Takano gives you 50/50 chance.

260
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:26,672
I'm confident that
I can cure you 100%.

261
00:18:27,973 --> 00:18:29,741
That's what I don't like it.

262
00:18:29,808 --> 00:18:31,009
Why?

263
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:34,546
I just don't like someone

264
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:39,218
who uses the word,
"100%" or "never" easily.

265
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,221
I never fail.

266
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:46,558
A doctor like that is the worst.

267
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:53,065
If a doctor lets me know the risk,

268
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:57,636
I will definitely trust him.

269
00:18:58,604 --> 00:19:03,775
So the doctor and a patient will
take responsibility and share the risk.

270
00:19:04,176 --> 00:19:06,912
What lies beyond risk is death.

271
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:12,217
That means the doctor assumes
the responsibility of my life.

272
00:19:13,385 --> 00:19:16,488
You claim 100% success

273
00:19:16,555 --> 00:19:19,191
because you don't
take responsibility of my life.

274
00:19:19,258 --> 00:19:20,092
don't you?

275
00:19:22,127 --> 00:19:24,596
That's my answer.

276
00:19:26,698 --> 00:19:28,033
You don't mind dying.

277
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,202
If I can die trusting.

278
00:19:31,403 --> 00:19:35,974
Dr. Takano is the only one
who can cut my stomach.

279
00:19:36,875 --> 00:19:41,446
He found my cancer.

280
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:46,485
Hey, can you give me some tea?

281
00:19:47,286 --> 00:19:49,421
There are fresh tea leaves
I received from Uji.

282
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,789
I won't do that.

283
00:20:03,001 --> 00:20:06,271
Oh well.Takano has been appointed
as Mrs. Asai's surgeon.

284
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:10,442
Mrs. Asai appointed him.

285
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:20,285
The most important surgery
was snatched! What's going on?

286
00:20:20,352 --> 00:20:21,587
I'm very sorry.

287
00:20:23,522 --> 00:20:24,656
Listen.

288
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:27,759
Never cooperate in
Takano's operation.

289
00:20:27,826 --> 00:20:31,063
Don't send any assistant
from our department.

290
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:32,464
Yes sir.

291
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:34,766
How about you Kondo?

292
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:36,401
Yes sir.

293
00:20:36,969 --> 00:20:39,204
Good. Answer me right now.

294
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:43,041
Prof. Hiruma is
on the edge of a cliff.

295
00:20:43,108 --> 00:20:45,410
Prof. Takano is trying
to kill this dept.

296
00:20:45,477 --> 00:20:48,580
Did we get in a wrong ship?

297
00:20:48,647 --> 00:20:50,882
Don't say such a thing.

298
00:20:50,949 --> 00:20:51,984
That's enough.

299
00:21:00,325 --> 00:21:04,029
Well, your method
isn't bad at all.

300
00:21:05,163 --> 00:21:08,467
However, I will be
in charge of this operation.

301
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:14,840
I read your "Living kidney and small
bowel exchange transplant."

302
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:16,975
That was great.

303
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:19,511
Thank you very much.

304
00:21:20,078 --> 00:21:23,649
So, will you be my assistant
for the operation?

305
00:21:24,916 --> 00:21:27,286
I know I can trust you.

306
00:21:37,262 --> 00:21:38,430
I decline.

307
00:21:39,665 --> 00:21:42,200
Not going to get on a winning horse?

308
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:46,104
Everyone here owes Professor Hiruma.

309
00:21:46,171 --> 00:21:48,640
No one will cooperate
in your operation.

310
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:52,411
Okay then.

311
00:21:55,447 --> 00:21:58,050
It's easier to change all staff.

312
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,822
That's so stupid.

313
00:22:05,957 --> 00:22:07,726
It's time to go home. See you.

314
00:22:09,594 --> 00:22:13,365
Daimon, wish I had a chance
to see your surgery.

315
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:16,034
Then can I be the surgeon?

316
00:22:17,536 --> 00:22:20,339
- Be my assistant.
- I won't do that.

317
00:22:24,076 --> 00:22:26,511
TEITO UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

318
00:22:26,578 --> 00:22:28,680
It's finally tomorrow.

319
00:22:29,247 --> 00:22:33,518
Can't wait to see the beautiful
firework before the election.

320
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:37,823
I'll be settled
with Prof. Hiruma tomorrow.

321
00:22:40,092 --> 00:22:41,326
I'm looking forward to it.

322
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,328
Yes, ma'am.

323
00:22:52,671 --> 00:22:54,606
It's a crab today?

324
00:22:56,141 --> 00:23:00,812
I received this
from my hometown of Kanazawa.

325
00:23:03,415 --> 00:23:05,350
- Would you like some?
- No thanks.

326
00:23:06,017 --> 00:23:08,653
Well...

327
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:12,557
It's a shame I can't eat
such a delicious food.

328
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:14,926
Not going to eat it?

329
00:23:14,993 --> 00:23:18,830
I have an operation tomorrow.

330
00:23:20,265 --> 00:23:21,099
Tomorrow?

331
00:23:21,166 --> 00:23:25,337
That's right. Dr. Takano told me
he'd do it tomorrow.

332
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:27,939
- I don't think you should.
- Why?

333
00:23:28,306 --> 00:23:29,908
Wait for a while.

334
00:23:30,942 --> 00:23:32,210
I don't think so.

335
00:23:32,277 --> 00:23:37,015
I hear the earlier the better
for cancer operation.

336
00:23:37,449 --> 00:23:40,819
Right? I think it's better.

337
00:23:41,253 --> 00:23:45,757
Dr. Takano has made time
to do the operation for me.

338
00:23:46,658 --> 00:23:50,929
He said this operation is
important to him, too.

339
00:23:50,996 --> 00:23:51,997
Ouch!

340
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:53,665
Oh, no.

341
00:23:54,566 --> 00:23:55,400
Are you alright?

342
00:23:55,467 --> 00:23:59,337
Nothing like this happened
to me before.

343
00:23:59,404 --> 00:24:00,772
It hurts.

344
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,575
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

345
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:08,613
Hi, Michiko.
You're late to come back.

346
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:10,182
It's so irritating.

347
00:24:10,248 --> 00:24:11,116
What happened?

348
00:24:11,183 --> 00:24:12,918
That lady upsets me.

349
00:24:12,984 --> 00:24:17,289
It's unusual to have a patient
that "I never fail" doesn't work.

350
00:24:17,355 --> 00:24:18,824
I see.

351
00:24:21,092 --> 00:24:23,228
Be assistants
for tomorrow's surgery.

352
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:25,497
- Who's surgery?
- That lady's.

353
00:24:25,564 --> 00:24:26,698
What's going on?

354
00:24:26,765 --> 00:24:29,701
You got that job?

355
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:30,602
That's great.

356
00:24:30,669 --> 00:24:33,171
- Bill the Internal Medicine.
- Internal Medicine?

357
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:42,747
Honored to have you as my assistant.

358
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:45,951
You insisted on doing it today.

359
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:52,190
Whatever the patient says,
I don't accept 50/50 chance.

360
00:24:52,257 --> 00:24:53,191
What are you saying?

361
00:24:54,726 --> 00:24:56,027
Can we cancel it today?

362
00:24:56,094 --> 00:24:58,330
- You can leave.
- I won't.

363
00:25:03,268 --> 00:25:07,439
Blood pressure 120/80,
and pulse is 99. Epidural is in.

364
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:10,742
So excited to
operate with you, Michiko.

365
00:25:10,809 --> 00:25:12,577
Don't make silly mistakes.

366
00:25:12,644 --> 00:25:13,678
We perform

367
00:25:13,745 --> 00:25:17,082
pancreaticoduodenectomy
with portal vein resection.

368
00:25:17,148 --> 00:25:19,351
- Scalpel.
- You're my assistant.

369
00:25:20,919 --> 00:25:22,821
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

370
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:30,028
- Ebina.
- Yes.

371
00:25:30,896 --> 00:25:34,165
Why is Daimon
from my department there?

372
00:25:34,232 --> 00:25:36,935
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

373
00:25:37,335 --> 00:25:42,073
The Internal Medicine Dept.
is in charge of this operation.

374
00:25:44,109 --> 00:25:45,877
- They are here.
- Okay.

375
00:25:45,944 --> 00:25:47,479
This way, please.

376
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:49,848
We've been expecting you.
Please sit.

377
00:25:50,282 --> 00:25:52,384
It's good to have you here, sir.

378
00:25:52,450 --> 00:25:56,555
Since this is the important
operation before the election,

379
00:25:57,355 --> 00:26:00,425
I thought
the board members should see it.

380
00:26:00,492 --> 00:26:02,561
That's a good idea.

381
00:26:02,627 --> 00:26:05,830
I hear we can see
the great operation, Hiruma.

382
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:06,731
Oh yes.

383
00:26:06,798 --> 00:26:09,801
Let's all observe the operation.

384
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:12,003
Yes, let's.

385
00:26:30,789 --> 00:26:32,457
It's 50/50 as I expected.

386
00:26:56,581 --> 00:26:59,618
Move the liver
and expand the operative field.

387
00:26:59,684 --> 00:27:00,885
Intestinal spatula.

388
00:27:03,588 --> 00:27:05,423
- Sweat.
- Excuse me, sir.

389
00:27:21,239 --> 00:27:24,342
Next we detach the mesocolon.

390
00:27:24,943 --> 00:27:26,344
- Forceps.
- Yes.

391
00:27:29,581 --> 00:27:30,582
I'm sorry.

392
00:27:32,851 --> 00:27:33,918
Professor Takano!

393
00:27:35,286 --> 00:27:36,955
- The stethoscope.
- Yes.

394
00:27:37,288 --> 00:27:41,459
Prof. Takano, do you hear me?
Do you hear me?

395
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:45,463
- What's happening?
- Prof. Hiruma.

396
00:27:46,765 --> 00:27:50,435
Prof. Takano, what happened?

397
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:52,570
State of shock.

398
00:27:52,637 --> 00:27:54,105
Can be strangulated ileus

399
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:55,473
- Do CT-scan.
- Yes.

400
00:27:58,376 --> 00:28:00,111
A stretcher to the Operating Room...

401
00:28:00,178 --> 00:28:02,180
I'll go downstairs.

402
00:28:02,247 --> 00:28:04,449
Stay. You don't have to go.

403
00:28:05,283 --> 00:28:07,952
Daimon, can you hear me? Daimon!

404
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:13,291
You take over Professor Takano

405
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:16,761
and perform surgery
on Mrs. Hisae Asai.

406
00:28:16,828 --> 00:28:19,931
The Internal Medicine
will take care of it.

407
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:24,836
Daimon. This is the order
from Executive Manager.

408
00:28:26,004 --> 00:28:27,005
Continue.

409
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,041
Daimon!

410
00:28:34,245 --> 00:28:36,815
- We have a stretcher. Come this way.
- Yes.

411
00:29:02,307 --> 00:29:03,608
Daimon.

412
00:29:05,477 --> 00:29:08,947
Don't worry about Takano.
Go on the surgery.

413
00:29:12,050 --> 00:29:17,021
Daimon. No cancer
you can't remove, right?

414
00:29:19,824 --> 00:29:21,259
Continue the operation.

415
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:37,442
We have a problem.

416
00:29:38,042 --> 00:29:40,445
Prof. Takano collapsed
and Dr. Daimon will continue.

417
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:42,680
- What?
- They need assistants.

418
00:29:42,747 --> 00:29:46,484
If we can save Mr. Asai's mother,
we'll have a bright future!

419
00:29:46,551 --> 00:29:48,119
- Let's go.
- Yes.

420
00:29:50,588 --> 00:29:53,124
SURGERY TIME

421
00:29:54,259 --> 00:29:57,729
Pancreaticoduodenectomy
with portal vein resection.

422
00:30:00,698 --> 00:30:01,566
Inoperative.

423
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:05,270
INOPERATIVE:
COMPLETE AS INOPERATIVE SURGERY

424
00:30:05,637 --> 00:30:06,471
Understood.

425
00:30:07,038 --> 00:30:08,673
- Absorbable suture.
- Yes.

426
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:12,911
Daimon, what are you saying?

427
00:30:13,745 --> 00:30:18,082
What do you mean by inoperative?
Daimon, don't sew her up.

428
00:30:18,783 --> 00:30:19,617
Daimon!

429
00:30:20,552 --> 00:30:24,422
Daimon, continue. Daimon!

430
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:26,858
Daimon!

431
00:30:26,925 --> 00:30:27,892
Daimon!

432
00:30:27,959 --> 00:30:31,996
Daimon! Listen! Hey, listen.

433
00:30:37,902 --> 00:30:40,471
Please put a mask on. Okay?

434
00:30:40,538 --> 00:30:41,773
I'll put it on for you.

435
00:30:42,407 --> 00:30:44,742
- Dr. Daimon, we'll help you.
- It's okay now.

436
00:30:46,311 --> 00:30:47,545
Professor Takano?

437
00:30:50,048 --> 00:30:52,951
Prof. Takano will be operated here.

438
00:30:53,384 --> 00:30:55,587
Mrs. Asai's ended as inoperative.

439
00:30:55,653 --> 00:30:57,222
What?

440
00:30:58,256 --> 00:30:59,224
What's the vital?

441
00:30:59,290 --> 00:31:01,759
Blood pressure is 115/70, pulse 95.

442
00:31:01,826 --> 00:31:04,128
- Start the urgent surgery
for ileus release.

443
00:31:04,195 --> 00:31:06,831
- Will we get into trouble?
- Yes, we will.

444
00:31:06,898 --> 00:31:10,201
- You didn't see me, alright?
- Thanks.

445
00:31:10,268 --> 00:31:11,402
- Monopolar.
- Here.

446
00:31:33,858 --> 00:31:35,960
Michiko Daimon.

447
00:31:39,264 --> 00:31:41,900
I will never ever forgive you.

448
00:31:44,135 --> 00:31:45,970
Never.

449
00:31:51,643 --> 00:31:53,912
Suture completes for mesocolon.

450
00:31:53,978 --> 00:31:56,247
I cut off the band
that strangulates ileum.

451
00:31:56,314 --> 00:31:57,081
- Metzen.
- Yes.

452
00:32:10,061 --> 00:32:11,562
Release strangulation complete.

453
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:17,101
No sign of necrosis in the S-shaped
mesocolon and in the ileum.

454
00:32:17,468 --> 00:32:20,471
- We'll start closing.
- Blood pressure 110/80. Normal pulse.

455
00:32:21,172 --> 00:32:22,774
Regular absorbable suture.

456
00:32:23,207 --> 00:32:25,777
SURGERY TIME

457
00:32:26,711 --> 00:32:28,379
- Blood loss?
- A small amount.

458
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:29,547
It's done.

459
00:32:39,791 --> 00:32:40,792
Good job, Doctor.

460
00:32:40,858 --> 00:32:43,328
- Good job.
- Good job.

461
00:32:47,832 --> 00:32:50,001
Why did you stop the surgery?

462
00:32:50,068 --> 00:32:52,370
No, I didn't.

463
00:32:53,604 --> 00:32:57,175
He'll be back to work in 10 days.

464
00:32:57,241 --> 00:32:58,710
I'm not talking about Takano.

465
00:32:58,776 --> 00:33:02,380
The patient wanted Dr. Takano
to do the operation. Not me.

466
00:33:04,349 --> 00:33:09,887
If I didn't save Dr. Takano, Mrs.
Asai's wish would never come true.

467
00:33:10,488 --> 00:33:11,422
That's it.

468
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:13,291
Don't mess with me.

469
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:25,503
Michiko Daimon.

470
00:33:28,806 --> 00:33:29,841
You're fired.

471
00:33:44,889 --> 00:33:47,759
Daimon. Are you a surgeon
in this department?

472
00:33:48,393 --> 00:33:51,629
You demean Prof. Hiruma as well as

473
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:53,197
the entire medical office.

474
00:33:54,298 --> 00:33:56,401
Why didn't you operate on Mrs. Asai?

475
00:33:57,502 --> 00:33:58,603
Answer me, Daimon!

476
00:33:59,670 --> 00:34:02,040
I'm scared of your face.

477
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:03,741
What?

478
00:34:04,308 --> 00:34:07,445
Why? You have the skill
to do it, Dr. Daimon.

479
00:34:09,213 --> 00:34:12,683
I just got fired. Good-Bye.

480
00:34:20,191 --> 00:34:22,760
Executive Manager doesn't see you.

481
00:34:23,761 --> 00:34:26,664
I apologize for my staff,
including Michiko Daimon,

482
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:29,634
was not able to perform

483
00:34:29,700 --> 00:34:31,302
to your expectation.

484
00:34:36,174 --> 00:34:37,642
Then go home.

485
00:34:37,708 --> 00:34:41,379
We'll charge
for assisting the special operation.

486
00:34:52,290 --> 00:34:54,759
Cut the crap. I never asked.

487
00:34:54,826 --> 00:34:56,394
Bill the Internal Medicine Dept.

488
00:34:56,794 --> 00:34:59,530
What about Dr. Takano's operation?

489
00:35:10,908 --> 00:35:11,809
Cut the crap.

490
00:35:11,876 --> 00:35:14,312
I won't pay one yen for him.

491
00:35:15,379 --> 00:35:16,881
I understand you're upset.

492
00:35:17,181 --> 00:35:21,986
Now you virtually lost
in the chairperson's election.

493
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,028
Pick a fight, bastards.

494
00:35:32,330 --> 00:35:33,464
I understood.

495
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:38,169
Wherever you go,
I hope you'll do business with us.

496
00:35:40,271 --> 00:35:42,006
Wait. Do you want to die?

497
00:35:54,018 --> 00:35:57,655
I envy part-timers.
They can do whatever they want.

498
00:35:58,456 --> 00:36:00,558
Prof. Takano was in emergency.

499
00:36:01,425 --> 00:36:04,629
That was the only way
she could save both.

500
00:36:04,695 --> 00:36:06,130
I don't care anymore.

501
00:36:06,197 --> 00:36:07,832
Mrs. Asai's operation

502
00:36:08,466 --> 00:36:10,668
will be done as soon as he recovers.

503
00:36:11,269 --> 00:36:14,605
We'll have no chance against him.
We're over.

504
00:36:19,110 --> 00:36:20,244
I feel like

505
00:36:21,445 --> 00:36:25,616
everything I worked for
is going down the drain.

506
00:36:27,051 --> 00:36:29,387
Life is in vain.

507
00:36:31,756 --> 00:36:32,957
After all,

508
00:36:33,758 --> 00:36:37,028
a doctor is
a corporate employee.

509
00:36:37,595 --> 00:36:38,496
Do you understand?

510
00:36:40,264 --> 00:36:41,666
We are just like them.

511
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:44,402
You are corporate employees, right?

512
00:36:44,769 --> 00:36:45,736
Listen.

513
00:36:46,103 --> 00:36:46,971
I am...

514
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:51,876
I'm a doctor,

515
00:36:51,943 --> 00:36:53,611
but I'm a corporate employee.

516
00:36:54,512 --> 00:36:57,448
I'm sorry. Dr. Ebina.

517
00:36:58,482 --> 00:36:59,917
I'm sorry.

518
00:37:01,185 --> 00:37:02,253
I apologize.

519
00:37:03,521 --> 00:37:05,122
I'm really sorry.

520
00:37:05,189 --> 00:37:06,557
Can I have one more drink?

521
00:37:09,193 --> 00:37:11,862
I'm so tired of it.

522
00:37:16,534 --> 00:37:20,271
Dr. Ebina, get a grip on yourself.

523
00:37:21,205 --> 00:37:22,873
You're so heavy.

524
00:37:30,681 --> 00:37:34,318
TABLE TENNIS COURT

525
00:37:37,488 --> 00:37:38,556
What's that?

526
00:37:39,090 --> 00:37:39,924
Why did you stop

527
00:37:40,358 --> 00:37:43,828
Asai's surgery, idiot!

528
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:48,733
Thanks to you,
I couldn't get any money.

529
00:37:49,333 --> 00:37:50,534
Pay me the fee

530
00:37:51,469 --> 00:37:54,138
for four assistants.

531
00:37:54,205 --> 00:37:56,741
Why me?

532
00:37:56,807 --> 00:38:01,012
Just find me another job.

533
00:38:38,416 --> 00:38:40,918
TABLE TENNIS COURT

534
00:38:48,326 --> 00:38:49,527
She's so free.

535
00:38:58,803 --> 00:39:00,071
How envious.

536
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:23,661
I guarantee her skill.

537
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:26,564
Please. Just for a trial.

538
00:39:27,331 --> 00:39:28,165
He hang up.

539
00:39:28,232 --> 00:39:31,502
- Not again.
- This was the 30th call.

540
00:39:31,569 --> 00:39:34,972
I'm afraid
if we'll find one in Kanto area.

541
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:37,375
Hiruma is putting a pressure.

542
00:39:38,909 --> 00:39:42,380
I'm having a withdrawal symptom.

543
00:39:42,446 --> 00:39:45,616
I want to do an operation!

544
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:48,219
I want to!

545
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:51,389
- Michiko.
- What?

546
00:39:51,455 --> 00:39:52,623
- Look.
- What?

547
00:39:58,863 --> 00:39:59,697
Oh, my God.

548
00:40:03,667 --> 00:40:04,702
It's been a while.

549
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:15,980
Prof. Takano returned
to work today and

550
00:40:16,614 --> 00:40:18,716
succeeded in Mrs. Asai's surgery.

551
00:40:18,783 --> 00:40:21,652
I'm an outsider now.

552
00:40:21,719 --> 00:40:25,489
If you had treated Mrs. Asai,

553
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:28,359
everything would've changed.

554
00:40:31,762 --> 00:40:35,566
The tide for the election
would've turned to Hiruma.

555
00:40:35,633 --> 00:40:37,835
and I would've been in troubles.

556
00:40:37,902 --> 00:40:41,505
Are you saying I lend you a hand?

557
00:40:43,874 --> 00:40:45,409
It's not too late.

558
00:40:46,177 --> 00:40:47,611
Why don't you work for me?

559
00:40:50,514 --> 00:40:52,416
I'll hire you.

560
00:40:54,351 --> 00:40:55,820
Let's rebuild this hospital.

561
00:40:56,487 --> 00:40:57,888
Thank you very much.

562
00:40:57,955 --> 00:41:02,059
I'll make a contract
without "I won't do that."

563
00:41:02,126 --> 00:41:03,427
I won't do that.

564
00:41:03,494 --> 00:41:06,263
Are you crazy?
This is a great offer.

565
00:41:06,330 --> 00:41:08,466
It's good Dr. Takano collapsed.

566
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:16,707
He knew the patient's cancer
had not become smaller yet.

567
00:41:28,519 --> 00:41:31,489
Did you know that, too?

568
00:41:34,725 --> 00:41:37,027
You still insisted on the operation

569
00:41:37,962 --> 00:41:39,597
because the election was coming.

570
00:41:42,566 --> 00:41:47,171
You used the operation
for the election

571
00:41:48,639 --> 00:41:52,843
by taking an advantage
of the patient who trusts you.

572
00:41:57,615 --> 00:41:59,016
Who do you think you are?

573
00:41:59,083 --> 00:42:01,285
- Michiko.
- I'm going out to eat.

574
00:42:01,352 --> 00:42:03,220
Michiko, wait.

575
00:42:03,754 --> 00:42:07,191
I apologize. I'll convince Daimon.

576
00:42:07,925 --> 00:42:10,194
Can you take care of her, please?

577
00:42:10,694 --> 00:42:13,097
What? What's this?

578
00:42:13,163 --> 00:42:13,998
No!

579
00:42:14,064 --> 00:42:20,738
I seriously hate cats.
Do something!

580
00:42:41,158 --> 00:42:43,594
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

581
00:42:43,661 --> 00:42:45,029
<i>Her medical certifications</i>

582
00:42:46,096 --> 00:42:51,201
<i>and on-the-job experience</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

583
00:42:53,971 --> 00:42:55,072
Stupid.

584
00:42:58,943 --> 00:43:01,211
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

585
00:43:02,546 --> 00:43:05,416
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

586
00:43:14,959 --> 00:43:17,494
I heard you're facing
an uphill battle for the election.

587
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,565
I apologize for making you worried.

588
00:43:22,466 --> 00:43:24,835
But we will bounce back.

589
00:43:25,936 --> 00:43:29,740
What we are giving out now
is a souvenir of this dinner.

590
00:43:29,807 --> 00:43:31,175
Please enjoy it.

591
00:43:35,980 --> 00:43:38,916
An election should be fair.

592
00:43:40,017 --> 00:43:41,518
You shouldn't do this.

593
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:46,523
I hope you like it.

594
00:43:46,590 --> 00:43:51,929
The sweet buns Prof. Hiruma brings
are good as always.

595
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:56,567
It's a special order, you know.

596
00:43:59,670 --> 00:44:01,071
I love it.

597
00:44:03,707 --> 00:44:05,242
I mean, the sweet buns.

598
00:44:30,134 --> 00:44:31,769
Hello?

599
00:44:37,207 --> 00:44:38,776
Oh, it's been a while.

600
00:44:39,810 --> 00:44:40,878
How have you been?

601
00:44:41,912 --> 00:44:42,846
What?

602
00:44:44,448 --> 00:44:45,683
To Daimon?

603
00:46:39,830 --> 00:46:42,065
THE STORY DEPICTED IN THIS DRAMA
IS FICTITIOUS

604
00:46:42,132 --> 00:46:44,468
- Can't anyone do it?
- I'll save you.

605
00:46:44,535 --> 00:46:46,136
Kondo, you're doing this.

606
00:46:46,203 --> 00:46:48,372
We got a confidential job.

607
00:46:48,438 --> 00:46:50,073
We won't have a double.

608
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:51,942
Even Daimon can't do this.

609
00:46:52,009 --> 00:46:53,877
Surgery is her last chance.

610
00:46:54,378 --> 00:46:57,014
I don't want to lose you, Michiko.
